               <div class="section is_transparent" style="">
                  <div class="section_content">
                     <td class="ou-value" colspan="2">
                        
                        <div class="section_heading">
                           <h2 id="students" class="heading is_ is_bottom is_left">D2L News for Students</h2>
                        </div>
                        
                        <p><strong>Students</strong><span><span>&nbsp;</span>may find detailed information about course availability, eCore/GoVIEW courses, D2L notifications, and updates to the D2L interface and functionality in the D2L Information for Students section.&nbsp;</span></p>
                        
                        <div class="section_heading">
                           <h3 class="heading is_">Getting Started in D2L for Students</h3>
                        </div>
                        
                        <p>Visit OwlTrain and watch <a title="Video introduction to D2L Brightspace for student in OwlTrain" href="https://ksu.percipio.com/linked-contents/e24a4503-693d-4fab-96d7-c466c21151dd/videoOnly" target="_blank" rel="noopener">this video</a> to learn more about KSU's online learning platform, D2L Brightspace.</p>
                        
                        <div class="section_heading">
                           <h3 class="heading is_">When can I see my courses in D2L?&nbsp;</h3>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="accordion_wrapper">
                           <ul class="accordion  is_">
                              <li class="accordion_item">
                                 <div class="accordion_title" id="title_d48e2906" aria-controls="content_d48e2906" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0" role="button">
                                    <p>Access to Previous Term Courses</p><i class="fas fa-plus open_close"></i></div>
                                 <div class="accordion_content" id="content_d48e2906" role="region" aria-labelledby="title_d48e2906">
                                    <div class="description">
                                       <td class="ou-content" contenteditable="true" colspan="2">
                                          
                                          <p>Courses will be visible to students in D2L until 60 days past the published end date of the course unless the end date has been adjusted by the instructor.&nbsp;</p>
                                          
                                          <p>If you can no longer access a KSU D2L course because the end date of the course has
                                             passed and you need access to the course, please reach out to the instructor of the
                                             course. If the instructor is not reachable, please reach out to the department where
                                             the course was offered.</p>
                                          </td>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </li>
                              <li class="accordion_item">
                                 <div class="accordion_title" id="title_d48e2937" aria-controls="content_d48e2937" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0" role="button">
                                    <p>Access to Future Term Courses</p><i class="fas fa-plus open_close"></i></div>
                                 <div class="accordion_content" id="content_d48e2937" role="region" aria-labelledby="title_d48e2937">
                                    <div class="description">
                                       <td class="ou-content" contenteditable="true" colspan="2">
                                          
                                          <p><strong>New Students</strong></p>
                                          
                                          <p>New students registered for an upcoming term will not have an account in D2L until
                                             courses for the upcoming term are loaded into D2L, approximately one month before
                                             the start of term. Once your account is created, you may log in, but you will not
                                             see your registered courses until the published start date of the course unless the
                                             start date has been adjusted by the instructor.</p>
                                          
                                          <p><strong>All Students</strong></p>
                                          
                                          <p>You will not see your registered courses in D2L until the published start date of
                                             the course unless the start date has been adjusted by the instructor. Start dates
                                             vary based on part of term. These dates may be found by visiting the<span>&nbsp;</span><a title="Academic Calendars web page" href="https://www.kennesaw.edu/registrar/academic-calendars/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Academic Calendars web page</a><span>&nbsp;</span>and navigating to the upcoming term.&nbsp;</p>
                                          </td>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </li>
                              <li class="accordion_item">
                                 <div class="accordion_title" id="title_d48e2982" aria-controls="content_d48e2982" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0" role="button">
                                    <p>Finding eCore Courses</p><i class="fas fa-plus open_close"></i></div>
                                 <div class="accordion_content" id="content_d48e2982" role="region" aria-labelledby="title_d48e2982">
                                    <div class="description">
                                       <td class="ou-content" contenteditable="true" colspan="2">
                                          
                                          <p>Your eCore courses will not be found in the KSU D2L Brightspace. Rather, you may find
                                             USG eCore courses by logging in to<span>&nbsp;</span><a title="link to GoVIEW" href="https://go.view.usg.edu/current-students/d2l/login" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Georgia Online Virtual Instruction Enterprise Wide (GoVIEW)</a>.&nbsp;</p>
                                          
                                          <p>For technical assistance, visit the<span>&nbsp;</span><a title="for eCore technical assistance" href="https://www.kennesaw.edu/ecore/contact-us.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KSU eCore contact page</a>. The KSU service desk will not be able to assist with login to eCore.&nbsp;</p>
                                          
                                          <p>To learn more about eCore courses visit the<span>&nbsp;</span><a title="KSU eCore home page" href="https://www.kennesaw.edu/ecore/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KSU eCore home page</a>.&nbsp;</p>
                                          </td>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </li>
                           </ul>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="section_heading">
                           <h3 class="heading is_">What's New in D2L?</h3>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="accordion_wrapper">
                           <ul class="accordion  is_">
                              <li class="accordion_item">
                                 <div class="accordion_title" id="title_d48e3247" aria-controls="content_d48e3247" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0" role="button">
                                    <p>January 2025 Updates - new D2L minimum supported browser information</p><i class="fas fa-plus open_close"></i></div>
                                 <div class="accordion_content" id="content_d48e3247" role="region" aria-labelledby="title_d48e3247">
                                    <div class="description">
                                       <td class="ou-content" contenteditable="true" colspan="2">
                                          
                                          <p>The January D2L Brightspace update increases the minimum supported browser versions
                                             to:</p>
                                          
                                          <ul>
                                             
                                             <li>Chrome 129</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Edge 129</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Safari 18</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Firefox 130&nbsp;</li>
                                             </ul>
                                          
                                          <p>The minimum legacy browsers are now:</p>
                                          
                                          <ul>
                                             
                                             <li>Chrome 94</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Edge 94</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Safari 15</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Firefox 92&nbsp;</li>
                                             </ul>
                                          
                                          <p>The following browsers are no longer supported:</p>
                                          
                                          <ul>
                                             
                                             <li>Chrome 67</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Edge 80</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Safari 12</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Firefox 67&nbsp;</li>
                                             </ul>
                                          </td>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </li>
                              <li class="accordion_item">
                                 <div class="accordion_title" id="title_d48e3312" aria-controls="content_d48e3312" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0" role="button">
                                    <p>August 2024 Updates</p><i class="fas fa-plus open_close"></i></div>
                                 <div class="accordion_content" id="content_d48e3312" role="region" aria-labelledby="title_d48e3312">
                                    <div class="description">
                                       <td class="ou-content" contenteditable="true" colspan="2">
                                          
                                          <p><strong>Email Status Field Removed from Review Assignment Submission Page</strong></p>
                                          
                                          <p>The<span>&nbsp;</span><em>email status field</em><span>&nbsp;</span>has been removed from the<span>&nbsp;</span><em>Review Assignment Submission</em><span>&nbsp;</span>page. You will no longer see a "Confirmation Email Sent Successfully" message when submitting an assignment. Email receipts are still sent and may be found in your inbox. Navigate to the Email Tool (envelope icon above Navbar) and filter by All Messages &amp; sort by newest date.&nbsp;</p>
                                          
                                          <p><strong>Minor Improvements to Discussions Tool Reading View</strong></p>
                                          
                                          <p>The Discussions Reading View has been improved in these ways:</p>
                                          
                                          <ul>
                                             
                                             <li>The<span>&nbsp;</span><em>Start New Thread</em><span>&nbsp;</span>button appears at both the top and bottom of the page to reduce scrolling.</li>
                                             
                                             <li>The<span>&nbsp;</span><em>Add Attachments</em><span>&nbsp;</span>section is opened by default and is wider on the screen.</li>
                                             </ul>
                                          
                                          <p><strong>Minimum Supported Browser Versions for D2L:</strong></p>
                                          
                                          <ul>
                                             
                                             <li>Chrome 124+</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Edge 124+</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Safari 17+</li>
                                             
                                             <li>Firefox 124+.</li>
                                             </ul>
                                          
                                          <p>The minimum legacy browsers are now: Chrome 81, Edge 81, Safari 14, and Firefox 75.</p>
                                          
                                          <p>The following browsers are no longer supported: Chrome 66, Edge 18, Safari 11, and
                                             Firefox 66.</p>
                                          
                                          <p><strong>SMS Notifications replaced by Pulse App</strong></p>
                                          
                                          <p>As of the end of July, D2L has removed the SMS Notifications service and any associated
                                             mobile numbers from the system. The email notification option within your D2L profile
                                             will continue to function, or you may continue to receive notifications on your mobile
                                             device by using the<span>&nbsp;</span><a title="knowledge base article for Pulse" href="https://kennesaw.service-now.com/sp?sys_kb_id=9f4ff7ce1bbd5510457cedf7b04bcbf8&amp;id=kb_article_view&amp;sysparm_rank=1&amp;sysparm_tsqueryId=6879024197030610c475f977f053af8d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pulse app</a>.</p>
                                          </td>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </li>
                              <li class="accordion_item">
                                 <div class="accordion_title" id="title_d48e3408" aria-controls="content_d48e3408" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0" role="button">
                                    <p>Previously Announced Updates</p><i class="fas fa-plus open_close"></i></div>
                                 <div class="accordion_content" id="content_d48e3408" role="region" aria-labelledby="title_d48e3408">
                                    <div class="description">
                                       <td class="ou-content" contenteditable="true" colspan="2">
                                          
                                          <div class="section_heading">
                                             <h4 class="heading is_">September 2023 Updates</h4>
                                          </div>
                                          
                                          <p><strong>Things to Know about Synchronous Quizzes</strong></p>
                                          
                                          <p>As announced in July, D2L now offers a Synchronous Quiz option where instructors may
                                             configure a quiz to start and end at the same time for all participants.</p>
                                          <strong>How does the new synchronous quiz type differ from the asynchronous quiz type?</strong>
                                          
                                          <ul>
                                             
                                             <li>The timer will begin to count down at the set start time whether you have accessed
                                                the quiz or not.</li>
                                             
                                             <li>If you enter the quiz that is set to auto-submit after the published start time, you will have the time remaining in the quiz available, not the full time allowance (as is the case with asynchronous).&nbsp;</li>
                                             </ul>
                                          
                                          <p><em>Example:</em><span>&nbsp;</span>A Synchronous quiz begins on October 1 at 10:00 AM and you have 30 minutes to complete the quiz, which will be automatically submitted at 10:30 AM. If you start the quiz at 10:10, you will have the remaining 20 minutes to work.&nbsp;</p>
                                          
                                          <p><em>Note:<span>&nbsp;</span></em>There are no special icons to indicate that a quiz is configured to be synchronous
                                             so pay careful attention to any instructions your professor may provide regarding
                                             synchronous quizzes.</p>
                                          
                                          <div class="section_heading">
                                             <h4 class="heading is_">July 2023 Updates</h4>
                                          </div>
                                          
                                          <p>Improvement to Quiz-taking Experience</p>
                                          
                                          <p>D2L has added a few new features to improve the quiz-taking experience:&nbsp;</p>
                                          
                                          <ul>
                                             
                                             <li style="list-style-type: none;">
                                                
                                                <ul>
                                                   
                                                   <li><strong>Quiz information</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>‚Äì previously seen only before starting a quiz but can now be accessed at any time during a quiz via a link</li>
                                                   
                                                   <li><strong>Improved Timing Communication</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>‚Äì addition of:

                                                      <ul>
                                                         
                                                         <li>option to hide the timer</li>
                                                         
                                                         <li>&nbsp;pop-up ‚Äútime remaining‚Äù warnings at intervals</li>
                                                         </ul>
                                                      </li>
                                                   
                                                   <li><strong>Quiz Results</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>‚Äì page shows confirmation of submission</li>
                                                   </ul>
                                                </li>
                                             </ul>
                                          
                                          <p>Minimum Versions for Supported Browsers</p>
                                          
                                          <p>The July update increases the minimum supported browser versions to: Chrome 112+, Edge 112+, Safari 16+, and Firefox 112+. The minimum legacy browsers remain at: Chrome 74, Edge 74, Safari 13, and Firefox 67. For an optimal experience that offers better performance, accessibility, and security, D2L recommends that all users access Brightspace with the latest version of their supported browser.&nbsp;</p>
                                          
                                          <p>Course Homepage May Look Different</p>
                                          
                                          <p>The default layout for course homepages has changed from a three-column layout to a two-column layout and now includes a widget near the bottom that gathers many important resource links for you. As always, course design may vary based on instructor preference.&nbsp;</p>
                                          </td>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </li>
                           </ul>
                        </div>
                        </td>
                  </div>
               </div>
            </div>
